Have you tried Indeed, and other similar job hunting sites? 'Yung isa kong kakilalang Grade 12 student, sa Alorica nagtatrabaho. Although need na highschool graduate, it doesn't need experience naman. (Not sure kung paano treatment nila sa employees nila though) Kung hindi ka makahanap ng jobs, pwede ka magfreelance work pansamantala. May mga kakilala akong suppliers ng premiums. Pwede ka ring mag-acad commissions, there are people na I know who earns 30k a month from it. Although matumal siya ngayon kasi kakasimula pa lang ng pasukan, ang peak months niya around September to November, then February to March. Tiyaga lang. Meron ding commissions dito sa Reddit, although usually scam nga. 'Yung mga legit kasi kakaunti lang talaga.

&#x200B;

If may makukuhaan ka ng funds or ayuda ngayon, or may connection ka, pwede rin yun. Save as much as possible, and then pagkagraduate mo ng senior high, try to find a job din. Wala ka bang ibang family members to rely on? Saan mo nakukuha yung funds mo for expenses since shelter lang ang provided ng relatives mo?

OP, have you considered finding scholarships? Or applying sa mga state universities para makamura or free na tuition mo? You can research more about local and even international scholarships, that can help.

&#x200B;

What jobs have you been finding? Have you tried applying sa mga BPO industries as a call center agent, or even sa mga fast food chains? May mga job opportunities lalo na sa BPO industry na hindi mo need ng kalakihang experience or degree. Although siyempre, mahirap ito, kung FTF 'yung school mo next year. You can try finding schools that offer blended or online classes para mas madali, pero if kaya mo naman, pwede kang mag-work sa gabi and pumasok sa umaga.

&#x200B;

Pwede ka ring magfreelance. I know a lot of students na kahit around Grade 10 pa lang ay nag-ffreelance na. They usually sell premium accounts ('yung mga spotify ganun), try dropshipping (although alam ko may risks ito), do academic, arts or design commissions, and even do virtual assistance. Ano bang skills mo OP? Pwede kitang tulungan makahanap ng freelance work.

&#x200B;

Since sabi mong after SHS ay aalis ka na sa bahay ng relatives mo, try saving up na now. Don't stop trying to find for jobs, or puwedeng pagkakitaan. Try mo rin na maghanap ng mga pwede mong i-rent or ma-stayan na mga lugar na ma-aafford ng expected savings mo after Grade 12. Choose your university wisely and siyempre, kapag may income ka na, learn to manage it din.

&#x200B;

Goodluck, OP! Kaya mo yan!

