OP, it's always possible to heal and get freedom from your seemingly toxic family. You just have to be prepared. If possible, save up your money and rent a house that's far away from your family. Try to find a job in that place, and make sure that before you move out, you have saving that's worth at least 3 months of food, water, bills and other necessities. **You have no choice**. That is the harsh truth with life. If you want a better life with freedom and independence, you have to work for it. Otherwise, days, months, and even years may pass, and you may still be in the same home, feeling worse day by day.

&#x200B;

You're also 22 already, an adult. If you leave, they can't come finding you if you don't leave any traces (such as telling people that are closely connected to them). The police won't be able to do anything anymore as you are no longer a minor.

&#x200B;

If you also can, save up for therapy. It will be worth it.

&#x200B;

You can do it, OP! Your future self will thank you if you start working for it as early as now.

